<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  /customer/address/new and /customer/address/edit — the address form as a
  PAGE. Figma 557:5173 (the form) inside 562:11026 (the account card).

  ===========================================================================
  WHY THIS PAGE HAS TO BE DESIGNED AT ALL
  ===========================================================================
  The dialog on the address book is the route a shopper normally takes, and it
  is easy to assume this handle is dead. It is not. It is reached:

    - with JavaScript unavailable or still loading, because the book's
      "اضف عنوان جديد" and "تعديل" controls are real links to it (that is
      deliberate; see address/spartrak-book.phtml);
    - by core's own Address\FormPost, which redirects to `*/*/edit` when a
      save fails validation — the route this store hit on the missing-city
      bug;
    - from a bookmark, a browser back button, or a mail link.

  Until now every one of those landed on Magento's stock two-column form:
  "CONTACT INFORMATION" / "ADDRESS" in English, with Street Address Line 1,
  Country, State/Province, City and Zip/Postal Code — five fields this
  storefront's design does not ask for, on a page no Figma frame draws.

  ===========================================================================
  IT IS THE SAME BLOCK AND THE SAME TEMPLATE AS THE DIALOG
  ===========================================================================
  `customer_address_edit` is core's Magento\Customer\Block\Address\Edit, kept
  whole: it resolves which address is being edited, applies the ownership
  check, restores posted data after a failed save, and supplies the save URL
  and the default-address flags. Only its template changes — to the exact file
  the dialog uses, so there is ONE address form on this site and not two that
  can drift apart.

  Core's own four arguments are left in place. This template does not read
  them, but a third-party module that adds a field to core's form does, and
  removing them would break that module on a page it has every right to
  extend.

  ===========================================================================
  THE CARD AROUND IT
  ===========================================================================
  The dialog gets its chrome from the modal widget. A page has none, so the
  form is MOVED inside a small template that draws the account card's header
  band — the same `.spartrak-account-card` every other page in this section
  uses. `<move>` rather than re-declaring the block: the block stays the one
  core created, with core's name, so anything referencing it by name still
  finds it.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="customer_address_edit" template="Magento_Customer::address/spartrak-form.phtml">
            <arguments>
                <!--
                  The governorate list, the configured country, and the readers
                  for the two values that are not plain AddressInterface
                  getters (the joined street text and the `additional_phone`
                  custom attribute). The same view model the dialog's own
                  handle injects.
                -->
                <argument name="address_form" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\CustomerAccount\ViewModel\AddressForm</argument>
            </arguments>
        </referenceBlock>

        <referenceContainer name="content">
            <block class="Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template"
                   name="spartrak.address.form.page"
                   template="Magento_Customer::address/spartrak-form-page.phtml"
                   cacheable="false"/>
        </referenceContainer>

        <move element="customer_address_edit" destination="spartrak.address.form.page" as="form"/>
    </body>
</page>
